[{:answer/id #uuid "b16070a9-1f2a-5f0a-9677-78ed81448fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\sin t, \\frac{1}{t}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197523} {:answer/id #uuid "b47cabab-bcf5-5ec7-9739-3287ae58f7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\sin t, \\frac{1}{t}, 2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197524} {:answer/id #uuid "d30777b3-f9d1-5748-b67d-509685486faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨ - \\sin t, \\frac{1}{t}, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197526} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb93243-ca2d-51b2-bf73-3d38248557ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨ - \\sin t, \\frac{1}{t}, 2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197527} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fc4589-9ea0-51e5-a1ef-7035649931ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - t, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197769} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fd3bda-be2f-5a45-9c7d-ca436531fee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197770} {:answer/id #uuid "185ee0a0-18d2-52e2-bbea-239f2a642d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197771} {:answer/id #uuid "1b18bb4f-97bd-5cf2-96b4-9b5ee39939f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197772} {:answer/id #uuid "72fcbeaf-400f-5dde-8ad4-b2e110797f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - t, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197773} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f83615-45a0-5f13-b8af-7e0bc8e482f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{-2}{t^{2} - 1},-25\\cos (5t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197781} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198227 :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198230 :question/id #uuid "c737d317-8e09-5ccb-b816-b5f56e925ba9" :question/math-academy-id "e-609" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199448 :tutorial/content "Differentiating vector-valued functions is easy: we just differentiate each component separately. So, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< x(t), \\, y(t) \\right>,\n$$\n\n then \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\mathbf{r} }{\\textrm dt}  = \\mathbf{r}'(t) = \\left< x'(t), \\, y'(t) \\right>.\n$$\n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< t+1, \\, t^2+2 \\right>,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGeometrically, the derivative of a vector-valued function $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t$ gives a vector that's tangent to the curve traced out by $\\mathbf r(t)$ at $t.$\n\n![](images/6d/6d7f1a972197ff5a92bb64bd0bab9e6dd779e800be48232124f8fda39fa3c949.png)\n\nLet's see some examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "2a3dd559-f60a-5a18-8d82-3dc93d7d7487" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1091 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199449 :tutorial/content "We can differentiate vector-valued functions with three components in the same way. \n\nFor example, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t) = \\big\\langle x(t), \\: y(t), \\: z(t) \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nis our vector-valued function, then the derivative is computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\text{d}\\mathbf{f}}{\\text{d}t} = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{ \\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, suppose that we are given the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\left\\langle t^3, \\:  \\ln(t+3), \\:  \\sqrt{t}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\n \n\nTo compute the derivative $\\mathbf f'\\!(t),$ we find the derivative of each component function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{d}{dt}⟨{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "f81076bc-29eb-53de-950f-4dd6e7b16816" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2110 :tutorial/title "Derivatives of Vector-Valued Functions"} {:answer/id #uuid "66acecfe-de86-5afc-988b-9f1070523b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257689} {:answer/id #uuid "6b27ee5e-014c-5fdf-9960-1dee281e352c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257727} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8fa841-78c3-5ab2-bed1-ff0215ecad07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257731} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b6986-fca0-55b7-ad52-a902a9fa6a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨{\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258835} {:answer/id #uuid "f6954e6f-e086-5f0e-bddb-8ea6239737d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{2}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258941} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66acecfe-de86-5afc-988b-9f1070523b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257689} {:answer/id #uuid "6b27ee5e-014c-5fdf-9960-1dee281e352c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257727} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8fa841-78c3-5ab2-bed1-ff0215ecad07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257731} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b6986-fca0-55b7-ad52-a902a9fa6a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨{\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258835} {:answer/id #uuid "f6954e6f-e086-5f0e-bddb-8ea6239737d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{2}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257727} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e09c224-5f2f-55b1-923a-f7806a571acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "be344af1-dfa6-5b94-ab32-51d8f42a61b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123171" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "05ab462d-d14d-5248-8b19-eecf34395231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263051} {:answer/id #uuid "2612d725-7382-53d5-aa60-70900b5c9b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263330} {:answer/id #uuid "435307ec-f4c4-50da-b4e9-2e9e7ed44854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263595} {:answer/id #uuid "77d85861-d061-57af-aea0-8ba92e48c360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t+1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264041} {:answer/id #uuid "df8d5feb-4951-5f97-ab2f-9278cfb12109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264940} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ab462d-d14d-5248-8b19-eecf34395231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263051} {:answer/id #uuid "2612d725-7382-53d5-aa60-70900b5c9b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263330} {:answer/id #uuid "435307ec-f4c4-50da-b4e9-2e9e7ed44854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263595} {:answer/id #uuid "77d85861-d061-57af-aea0-8ba92e48c360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t+1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264041} {:answer/id #uuid "df8d5feb-4951-5f97-ab2f-9278cfb12109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263051} :answer-field/id #uuid "582fbd73-f550-5fee-835b-21523deda1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4815588-6450-5555-83dd-11960a205f75" :question/math-academy-id "q-130390" :question/problem "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c08e415-1582-566c-abca-01f98220019c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299994} {:answer/id #uuid "1cacc6ae-6c30-5cef-af1f-99f16fec5988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300094} {:answer/id #uuid "4abdc31a-a0b8-56f6-9d09-328a2a8e3d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300345} {:answer/id #uuid "8dff7ef7-14fa-540d-9f26-e1581a5dc18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300682} {:answer/id #uuid "99c862a2-d0f6-5006-9548-657c2bc2cea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300733}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300345} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf36595-db23-5508-b678-6942ff38d4fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f8539782-987e-5a96-b997-ff8444e6065b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32416" :question/problem "Calculate the second derivative of  $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,{s}^{4}+10s,\\,55⟩$ with respect to $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{4}+10s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(55)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,4{s}^{3}+10,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the second derivative by differentiating ${f}^{′}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4{s}^{3}+10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,12{s}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93f1240f-0b47-5a56-8794-998240849da8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318068}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318068} :answer-field/id #uuid "4162dbda-4b92-5f56-a521-c6ed9fa88ef4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76602505-6314-5889-af6f-473838f62468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317970} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae6e1aaa-dcf3-5b7d-8951-e90b6b6f06b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94125aec-27df-5037-a264-fdd046612e1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347619" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t}-4,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36927d02-05fb-5b03-9115-266e87dfb2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317741}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317741} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9c5c6a-9e59-5ab2-90e4-786826c7f74d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29a40cd-f42b-59f9-88b1-1014aea10417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318123} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa3843c-bd78-5f95-bb2e-1f9ae549c2b5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee41193-91a4-59e5-9a2a-3ee0e67f6f8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318051} :answer-field/id #uuid "b65cb892-96d0-5018-80ac-5a27a61abc59" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "32510c9a-1b3e-55bf-9f6f-36e2f15f8326" :question/math-academy-id "q-347628" :question/problem "Given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t),\\,{t}^{3}⟩,$ what is ${f}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83a93010-66f9-5f63-a619-5ae6f0ba5901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318011} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b7c75a-6b0f-5c4c-82e5-e4a6e779fcee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4b7b95ab-a56a-58eb-ba8d-91d73cfdc4f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-350217" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(-1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(-1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "3eee4af2-0248-5ce4-b7f6-6fee6d1a8fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} {:answer/id #uuid "5e338882-ec9b-52c8-9509-458d83a50da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330790} {:answer/id #uuid "60877467-26a5-565e-9a60-7a1ac5cca6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330808} {:answer/id #uuid "662007e1-aa2b-54ce-b04c-f2ad08993265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330861} {:answer/id #uuid "6687452e-ac8c-536f-9456-54fd1b9619f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330866} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9e1b5e-3926-5b9a-ae3b-e6b881cd6740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330907} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc6346e-b150-5374-a32d-4d1a5ec7bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330933} {:answer/id #uuid "712abd91-42eb-5ec8-84bf-b6f634404a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} {:answer/id #uuid "86448057-4fd0-59f3-ba66-fd86d9b805be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331142} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd3b07d-2774-58fa-93e9-db174c995ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331226} {:answer/id #uuid "d2236804-95e9-51ec-8331-608fbaf4e7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045