ref 17592186332820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eee4af2-0248-5ce4-b7f6-6fee6d1a8fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} {:answer/id #uuid "662007e1-aa2b-54ce-b04c-f2ad08993265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330861} {:answer/id #uuid "6687452e-ac8c-536f-9456-54fd1b9619f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330866} {:answer/id #uuid "712abd91-42eb-5ec8-84bf-b6f634404a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd3b07d-2774-58fa-93e9-db174c995ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331226}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d43db0b-4e5d-5721-97a5-e44ef07baae7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "830e243e-5841-5ab7-af4b-a130c74364b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-50409" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{\\sin }^{3}⁡t,\\,{\\cos }^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={\\sin }^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={\\cos }^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41aac7b0-e36a-52aa-883e-d2ddfd33ab74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} {:answer/id #uuid "5e338882-ec9b-52c8-9509-458d83a50da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330790} {:answer/id #uuid "8489b988-e5d3-5081-88ab-f63b44492691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331127} {:answer/id #uuid "f89ff7dc-52c8-5018-b8e3-07b4fec5c000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332135} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfbc103-aa8d-5079-8217-c29c118b141a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22c019a-4532-5eef-bb3c-f171fa627817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "90f83aed-c049-593e-9f58-73c0262de78f" :question/math-academy-id "q-50411" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c4f3a69-92f8-593d-a5d5-10afbe7a1536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(t)-{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387348} {:answer/id #uuid "59ff0643-9755-5655-9e7a-c6a58bcc6ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡t+{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387349} {:answer/id #uuid "d4dbbc4f-0523-5ed7-98a6-d97ffa12a2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387350} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3ab8fd-29e4-55fd-ab10-4110925db260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(2t)+{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387351} {:answer/id #uuid "83af61a3-eb17-5200-919f-b41643d2b386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387352}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387351} :answer-field/id #uuid "21580012-8c25-5076-900b-45885ca5b66a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b02b05ec-3c49-5ba7-a525-3faa0181bc7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123184" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t) \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){\\tan }^{2}⁡(2t)+4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(2t)+{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{3}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(2t)+{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4f3a69-92f8-593d-a5d5-10afbe7a1536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡(t)-{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387348} {:answer/id #uuid "59ff0643-9755-5655-9e7a-c6a58bcc6ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({\\tan }^{2}⁡t+{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387349} {:answer/id #uuid "d4dbbc4f-0523-5ed7-98a6-d97ffa12a2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186