#edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6d3b1235-338f-544b-9e5f-ca61081e2c9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130408" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1},\\,(t+2)^{2}⟩$ at $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+2)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},\\,2(t+2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1fe797-2919-5ad5-93f4-36e98939c7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388106} {:answer/id #uuid "e466e53d-149c-525e-ba62-5068da1d66a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388107} {:answer/id #uuid "f3dc9d67-7e06-5b29-a02d-e5f0b4cf4be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi -2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388109} {:answer/id #uuid "0f95bba9-b5f0-5dff-8ca4-f870c2f23413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2\\pi ⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388110} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fde686e-0040-50c8-9b9b-1ad4f1e8aaa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{